# Patterns to ignore when building packages (helm package / helm
# dependency update). Unlike .gitignore, this controls what gets bundled
# into the .tgz a downstream consumer (my-crd) pulls in via file:// — so
# it matters for more than repo hygiene: without excluding harness/ here,
# every downstream `helm dependency update` repackages crdkit's ENTIRE
# directory tree, including harness/'s own charts/crdkit-0.0.0.tgz (its
# bundled copy of crdkit, from testing the harness locally) — which
# itself may contain a stale, even-earlier-nested copy, growing with
# every local test cycle. This exact recursive bloat once pushed a
# packaged crdkit past 5MB and broke helm-unittest's file-size limit in
# my-crd-test. harness/ and tests/ are crdkit's own local dev/test
# scaffolding — a downstream consumer never needs either.
harness/
tests/

# Common VCS dirs
.git/
.gitignore
.helmignore

# Common backup files
*.swp
*.bak
*.tmp
*.orig

# Various IDEs
.project
.idea/
*.tmproj
.vscode/
.DS_Store
